<title>HUNGARY: Hungary two-yr govt-bond yield falls to 18.58 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary two-yr govt-bond yield falls to 18.58 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's two-year government bonds was set by auction at 18.58 percent, down from 20.56 percent at an auction on January 2, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    BONDS OF THE 1999/E SERIES   HTBJ</p>
<p>    Date of issue		 9 January 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 January 1999</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    35,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     69,758.50 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   35,000 million forints @</p>
<p>    Total issued		38,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  18.58 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		  102.64 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a fixed interest of 19.50 percent to be paid twice yearly, on January 12 and July 12.</p>
<p>    Interest payment     Date			Percent</p>
<p>				 12 July 1997	    9.83</p>
<p>				 12 January 1998	 9.83</p>
<p>				 12 July 1998	    9.67</p>
<p>				 12 January 1999	 9.83 @</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
